{
	title: 'Plain-value settings with plugin.set',
	spec: `Settings that are constants are plain values on module objects (\`ttlMs: 3_600_000\`, read as \`models.ttlMs\`), not zero-argument functions. Code reads them through the object at call time, never destructured or captured at import. Values that compute something (read config.ason, derive from other values) stay functions.

plugin.set(obj, key, value) overrides a plain value with the same ownership as hooks: removed on reload, delete or expiry; when several files set one key the last in filename order wins, and removing it reveals the earlier one, then the original exactly. Its type allows only non-function keys and checks the value type; a missing or function key is a load error naming file and target (use around). /plugins lists it as "<module>.<key> set". Like hooks, set affects only future reads; repaints go through onChange.

Docs: README "Plugins" section, tasks/README.md module conventions and plugins/example-plugin.ts describe set and the plain-value rule.`,
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['an'],
	foldInto: ['an']
}
